  plant in the second half of the week  this is also consistent with  announcement  announcements that the agency made  some days ago a lot of observers  expected the trip to be imminent  especially after putin gave up his  opposition to the idea of the  inspectors traveling through  non-occupied territory in ukraine  here in ukraine the observers the  inspectors the team of experts they are  definitely very welcome  and people here are seriously concerned  about a possible disaster  there have been reports  regarding  power outages over the weekend new power  outages and also renew renewed fighting  directly around the plant in the past 24  hours  jan phillip there have been  contradictory accounts from ukraine and  russia about what's going on at the  zaparia plant is there any way to verify  what's actually happening  international reporters can't travel to  the site at the moment so there is no  possibility to verify the information  firsthand however we have talked to many  employees that are still working at the  plant and we've also talked to the  town's mayor where the plant is located  at the same time we have russia's  history of  systematic disinformation  disinformation that can easily be  falsified so we can almost say for  certain that russia is using the plant  as a military basis and that there have  been false flag attacks by russia on the  planet but having said this uh there are  also strong indications that uh  ukrainian troops have attacked the plant  several times in the past  weeks and also the town's mayor didn't  deny that there have been ukrainian  attacks around the plant  jan philip we've seen in the report and  you've mentioned as well there's  obviously concerns about radiation what  do we know though about the radiation  levels at the plant  the good news is that the recent  measurements  at the plant and  very close to the plant have all been  within the normal range and the  emergency systems seem to be in place as  we heard in the report authority in the  report authorities are continuing to  distribute iodine iodine tablets so  there is no  way to say everything is okay but the  radiation levels are in normal range at  the moment and everybody is looking  forward for the team of international  experts to arrive  thank you jan phillip jan philipp  schultz in kiev  despite its major military efforts  russia's territorial gains in eastern  ukraine have been limited uw  correspondent young philip schultz  traveled to a frontline region where he  met ukrainians trying to get on with  their lives despite the dangers they  regularly face  we're on the road in eastern ukraine 20  kilometers from the front line in the  last small town before the combat zone  signs of war are all around  at the local supermarket soldiers do  their weekly grocery shopping before  heading back to the trenches  the situation is tense in recent days  the russians have stepped up their  attacks  in this semi-abandoned front-line town  diana and alina want to serve the best  cappuccino east of kiev  we hear the missiles flying over us and  we hear them exploding it's scary  it sounds always so terrifying but we  try to get on with our work  at first their small conflict zone cafe  was an insider tip now soldiers often  queue up outside for half an hour of  peace and a slice of homemade cake  when we get a break from the fighting we  come straight here for coffee  diana is proud that they haven't closed  their cafe for a single day since the  war started only once have they been  forced to take evasive action when  russian strikes came really close and  people ran for shelter  when we heard the shelling we went to  hide in a safe space after a few minutes  we went back to work  the women have set up their own small  emergency aid center directly above the  cafe  here they collect food medicine and  hygiene products for families fleeing  the surrounding villages some of it is  donated some they buy with their own  money  we especially try to help the smaller  children who arrive here from the  occupied territories we have everything  diapers clothes toys all the things they  need to feel better  diana and alina have got used to working  in a cafe on the front line still they  hope one day to use the emergency room  again for its original purpose having a  good time
 

